&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Beast Industries is a media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, known&amp;nbsp;as MrBeast, the most-watched creator in the world. What started as a YouTube channel is now&amp;nbsp;a global company spanning digital media, consumer products, philanthropy, technology,&amp;nbsp;financial services, and original streaming content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Our teams move fast, think big, and take ownership. We chase ambitious ideas, execute&amp;nbsp;relentlessly, and are building something that has never existed before. We are a uniquely&amp;nbsp;multi-generational team of creators, operators, and builders across very different businesses,&amp;nbsp;and we only win if everyone is connected to the same mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Beast Industries is growing quickly, and we need someone to own how our people understand&amp;nbsp;our mission and goals, embrace the products and services we’re building (and the “why” behind&amp;nbsp;them), get company information and stay connected to each other.. You&#39;ll build our internal&amp;nbsp;communications function from scratch as a system, not a stream of tactics, so every employee&amp;nbsp;understands where we&#39;re headed, sees how their work connects to the mission, and knows&amp;nbsp;what&#39;s expected of them. You&#39;ll also make sure they hear about big changes from us, clearly&amp;nbsp;and early, and in ways that are authentic to our culture.&amp;nbsp;You&#39;ll work closely with executive leadership to build and carry the story of the company,&amp;nbsp;translating strategy into a mission every employee can repeat in their own words. You&#39;ll connect&amp;nbsp;teams across our businesses, our offices and remote employees, build trust in senior&amp;nbsp;leadership, ensure no information gaps exist, and highlight the work our teams do every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll meet an employee audience that uses a mix of written, video, audio, live, and mobile&amp;nbsp;formats daily, so our communications must be designed to meet them where they are.&amp;nbsp;You&#39;re an excellent writer and a sharp advisor to executives. You have a strong point of view on&amp;nbsp;how to communicate well, and you&#39;re just as eager to hear a better idea. You can make&amp;nbsp;complicated things simple, stay honest and direct when the news is hard, and pair empathy with&amp;nbsp;data to understand what&#39;s landing with employees. You reason from first principles: you ask&amp;nbsp;what problem a message or channel is solving before choosing the format, then test, learn, and&amp;nbsp;retire what doesn&#39;t work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;This role reports to the Chief Communications Officer and partners with the CEO, Chief People&amp;nbsp;Officer, General Counsel, CFO, and business unit Presidents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4 class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Internal Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Set the vision and strategy for internal communications across Beast Industries, and run it day to day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Define the mission narrative: the single story that connects company strategy, quarterly priorities, and each team&#39;s work, so any employee can answer &quot;why does my work matter?&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Create regular touchpoints, like all-hands and leadership updates, that employees can count on, on a published weekly, monthly, and quarterly cadence, with a clear standard for how quickly decisions are shared.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Help executives communicate in their own voice while keeping messages consistent across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Build a manager cascade to equip people managers with the messaging, materials and context they need to ensure key announcements and people/HR related changes are communicated effectively throughout all levels of the organization. In success, this cascade will establish managers as one of our most trusted channels for information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Find and close information deserts: diagnose which teams, locations, tenure groups, and roles are consistently last to know, and fix the gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Design a multi-format channel strategy that considers audience preferences across business units and roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Create two-way channels, including pulse surveys, and a visible &quot;you said, we did&quot; loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Executives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Be a trusted advisor to senior executives and functional leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Draft CEO communications, including announcements, org updates, talking points, remarks, presentations, FAQs, and video scripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Lead communications for tentpole, company-wide People team initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Prepare executives for town halls, employee Q&amp;amp;As, and other high-stakes moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Coach executives to explain the why behind decisions, not only announce them, and set a leadership communications rhythm (for example, CEO office hours, fireside chats, and a regular leadership letter).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Through Change&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Plan communications for reorganizations, leadership transitions, and other major changes so employees get clarity and uncertainty stays low. Build and maintain playbooks for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Work with the CCO, HR, Legal, Finance, and leaders on sensitive employee communications, including confidentiality protocols that balance transparency with legal and security needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Hold a standard of ethical, honest communication on hard news, including mistakes, rumors, and what we don&#39;t yet know.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Create comms programs that reinforce our values and bring teams closer together, and make our high-performance expectations clear: what great looks like, how we give feedback, and how we experiment, fail fast, and learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Own leadership forums, AMAs, recognition programs, and engagement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Tell employee and team stories, including through video and audio, produced in partnership with our in-house creative teams, that celebrate our people and milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Design the communications arc for new-hire onboarding and rapid growth, so every new employee feels connected to the mission from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure What Works&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Set metrics for internal communications, track them consistently and share regularly with leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Use engagement data and employee feedback to improve our channels, cadence, and content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Run small, regular experiments on formats, timing, and channels; keep what works and retire what doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;8+ years in internal communications, executive communications, change management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience building or leading internal communications at a high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Outstanding writing, editing, and storytelling, across different audiences and formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;A track record advising executives and influencing senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience leading communications through growth, transformation, or organizational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Sound judgment and discretion with confidential information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Strong project management and the ability to juggle multiple high-priority projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience designing new communications systems from the ground up, experimenting, measuring the results and using them to improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Comfort leading cross-functional work as an individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience communicating across generations, locations, and roles, including remote, global, and non-desk employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience producing multimedia content, including video and audio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Experience in media, gaming, technology, the creator economy, or consumer brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Familiarity with tools like Slack, Notion, Workvivo, SharePoint, and Google Workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Comfort in visible, fast-moving environments where priorities change quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success in Your First Year&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;By Day 90: Developed a topline 2027 internal narrative arc, Audited current channels, assessed business unit needs, mapped where information gaps exist, established a manager cascade process and launched a published companywide cadence calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;By Month 6: Internal narrative is live, baseline metrics are established and aligned on with leadership and companywide cadence of comms is being tested and refined. Launched an internal communications strategy and core programs that employees rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Became a trusted advisor to executive leadership on employee communications. Raised employee engagement with company communications and understanding of company priorities, with clear metrics to show it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Created playbooks for major company moments, like reorgs and leadership changes. Built stronger connections across teams and offices, with a measurable increase in satisfaction with information access and communication across all groups.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Beast Industries?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At Beast, communication is how we keep people connected to the mission and to each other. You&#39;ll build this function from the start, work directly with the leaders shaping the company&#39;s future, and help one of the fastest-growing entertainment companies in the world stay close as it grows. If you thrive in fast-moving environments and love turning complex strategies into messages people care about, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Target total compensation ranges from &lt;strong&gt;$270,000 to $350,000&lt;/strong&gt;, including a fixed annual salary of &lt;strong&gt;$180,000 to $230,000&lt;/strong&gt;, a discretionary annual cash bonus, plus an employee equity grant and comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Perks, Why Work On the MrBeast Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are redefining what entertainment and storytelling look like at global scale. Every piece of content we publish reaches millions and influences culture in real time. This is your opportunity to lead the team that decides how those moments come to life across every screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Medical (Blue Cross Blue Shield), Dental, Vision and company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions to employee Health Savings Accounts (HSA)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Plan with Safe Harbor company-matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy and paid company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-provided technology package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation assistance where applicable, including travel and company-provided housing for the first 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn strategic partnerships into marketing programs that accelerate the next generation of Beast Industries businesses.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is building a new telecommunications and mobile business designed for the next generation of consumers. The Director of Mobile Marketing will lead the day-to-day marketing operations, go-to-market execution, and subscriber-growth programs supporting that business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Viral Marketing, this role will translate established business, brand, and viral marketing strategies into detailed execution plans across customer acquisition, lifecycle marketing, retail, CRM, partner channels, and subscriber communications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a focused operating role dedicated to the telecommunications and mobile category. It is not responsible for setting the broader viral marketing vision for Beast Industries, leading the marketing strategy for other Beast businesses, or developing the company’s flagship creative platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success requires deep telecommunications or subscription-marketing expertise, strong operational discipline, and the ability to coordinate complex programs across internal teams and external partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Mobile Marketing will serve as the senior operational marketing leader for Beast Industries’ telecommunications and mobile business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will be responsible for converting approved strategies and creative platforms into executable go-to-market programs that drive subscriber acquisition, activation, engagement, retention, referrals, and household growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines telecommunications or subscription-marketing experience with strong capabilities in product commercialization, lifecycle marketing, retail activation, CRM, performance measurement, and cross-functional program management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This leader should be highly effective at managing complex execution, establishing clear operating rhythms, and ensuring that marketing commitments are delivered accurately, efficiently, and on schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile Go-to-Market Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development and execution of go-to-market plans for the Beast Industries telecommunications and mobile business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate approved business, brand, and viral marketing strategies into detailed launch plans, workstreams, timelines, budgets, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate marketing execution for mobile plans, pricing changes, promotional offers, service features, device programs, upgrades, trade-ins, and customer benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear customer-facing communications explaining plan value, pricing, switching processes, service features, and member benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all launches are supported by appropriate operational, retail, CRM, customer-service, legal, and partner readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subscriber Acquisition&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute customer-acquisition programs within the approved mobile marketing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage conversion initiatives across digital, retail, affiliate, referral, CRM, paid media, and partner channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with analytics and finance teams to monitor acquisition performance and improve conversion efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify friction within the customer journey and recommend improvements to enrollment, activation, and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize approved campaigns and offers based on performance data and customer behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifecycle and Retention Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational development of customer onboarding, engagement, retention, renewal, win-back, and referral communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build CRM journeys across email, SMS, app, web, and other owned customer channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and customer-experience teams to improve activation, engagement, and long-term customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop programs that reduce preventable churn and increase plan participation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the lifecycle calendar and ensure that communications are coordinated across customer touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Household and Referral Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute approved referral, family-plan, household-expansion, and member-get-member programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage incentive structures, customer communications, operational requirements, and campaign timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor referral participation, household conversion, and related subscriber-growth metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend optimizations based on program performance without altering the underlying strategic or creative platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with product, legal, finance, and customer operations to ensure offers are executable and compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail and Distribution Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day coordination of retail and distribution marketing for the mobile business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop retail toolkits, merchandising requirements, sales materials, employee communications, and launch-readiness plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with telecommunications partners and retail teams to ensure accurate execution across participating locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support seasonal retail events, device launches, promotional periods, and customer-conversion initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor retail performance and identify opportunities to improve customer education and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Marketing Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the day-to-day mobile marketing workstreams with the designated telecommunications partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert approved partnership commitments into detailed marketing calendars, deliverable trackers, approval processes, and launch plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain visibility into contractual marketing obligations, deadlines, dependencies, and partner requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare materials and reporting for senior partner reviews led by the Head of Viral Marketing and other Beast Industries executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate strategic, commercial, creative, or relationship issues to the Head of Viral Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain productive working relationships with partner marketing, retail, product, legal, analytics, and operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign Implementation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize approved creative and viral marketing platforms across mobile customer touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop execution briefs for agencies, production partners, media teams, CRM teams, retail teams, and other functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage asset requirements, production schedules, partner approvals, trafficking, localization, and launch readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all campaign materials align with the approved strategy, creative direction, and Beast Industries brand standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate campaign implementation without assuming ownership of enterprise creative strategy or platform development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement and Optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reporting for subscriber acquisition, activation, conversion, retention, churn, referrals, household growth, CRM engagement, retail performance, and campaign efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with analytics and finance teams to develop accurate performance dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular performance updates to the Head of Viral Marketing and relevant business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify executional improvements and make recommendations grounded in customer and performance data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct post-launch reviews and incorporate learnings into future mobile marketing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish disciplined operating rhythms across mobile marketing workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain integrated calendars, project plans, decision logs, approval trackers, risk registers, and status reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clarify ownership, deadlines, dependencies, and escalation paths across internal teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify executional risks early and coordinate solutions with the appropriate functional owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable processes that allow the mobile business to manage multiple campaigns, offers, and launches efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a focused team supporting mobile go-to-market execution, lifecycle marketing, retail coordination, and marketing operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear roles, responsibilities, goals, and performance expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop team capabilities in telecommunications marketing, subscription growth, CRM, retail execution, and program management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain close alignment with the Head of Viral Marketing and operate within the strategic and creative direction established by that office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–12 years of progressive marketing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in telecommunications, wireless, mobile, subscription services, or an adjacent category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in mobile go-to-market execution, subscriber marketing, lifecycle marketing, CRM, retail marketing, or growth operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience supporting customer acquisition, activation, retention, referral, and household-growth programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating marketing programs with telecommunications carriers, retailers, distribution partners, or large enterprise organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of mobile-plan economics, switching behavior, device programs, promotional offers, customer onboarding, and churn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex cross-functional initiatives involving product, retail, customer service, analytics, finance, legal, operations, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational and program-management capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate approved strategies into detailed, executable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing agencies, production partners, CRM teams, media teams, and other external resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated comfort working with performance data and marketing analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced environment with evolving priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with creator-led brands or entertainment businesses is helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The target total compensation for this role ranges from &lt;strong data-start=&quot;217&quot; data-end=&quot;255&quot;&gt;$250,000 to $380,000&lt;/strong&gt;, including a fixed annual salary of &lt;strong data-start=&quot;292&quot; data-end=&quot;316&quot;&gt;$200,000 to $260,000&lt;/strong&gt;, an annual performance bonus, participation in our employee equity plan, plus comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Perks, Why Work On the MrBeast Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are redefining what entertainment and storytelling look like at global scale. Every piece of content we publish reaches millions and influences culture in real time. This is your opportunity to lead the team that decides how those moments come to life across every screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Medical (Blue Cross Blue Shield), Dental, Vision and company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions to employee Health Savings Accounts (HSA)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Plan with Safe Harbor company-matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy and paid company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-provided technology package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation assistance where applicable, including travel and company-provided housing for the first 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beast Industries is looking for a Director of Apparel Design, who is equally creative and a strategizer. This isn&#39;t a role for someone who wants to delegate the creative work and only manage a team, &amp;nbsp;it is a role where you will be driving and creating it.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll own the full design vision for our apparel line, with a focus on kids&#39; lifestyle products and an eye toward adult categories. Working closely with the Head of Product, you&#39;ll set the seasonal direction, collaborate with the whole product team, and produce original garments built to last. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Design &amp;amp; Development&lt;br&gt;Lead original silhouette design across kids&#39; and adult lifestyle and athletic categories, from initial sketch through production-ready tech pack&lt;br&gt;Produce detailed technical sketches that communicate construction intent; panel layouts, topstitching, stitch lines, seam placements, so developers can execute without guesswork&lt;br&gt;Own the construction pages within tech packs, bringing a level of technical rigor that reduces back-and-forth with factories&lt;br&gt;Work directly with the Graphic Designer on placement, scale, and colorway for graphic applications, ensuring the apparel and graphics read as a cohesive product&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Creative Direction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Build and manage the seasonal design calendar, planning the full year of apparel development with clear milestones&lt;br&gt;Lead trend and design research to inform product direction and keep the brand ahead of the market&lt;br&gt;Monitor the apparel landscape in streetwear, sportswear, &amp;amp; youth fashion industries, to translate emerging trends into product decisions. You&#39;ll recommend which specific styles, silhouettes, fabrics, and details we should be executing each season&lt;br&gt;Present seasonal concepts and design strategy to senior leadership with clear creative rationale and commercial context&lt;br&gt;Establish scalable design processes as the team grows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Manage and develop the design team, providing clear creative direction and building toward a stronger team over time&lt;br&gt;Partner with product development, sourcing, and marketing teams to ensure designs are technically viable and delivered on schedule&lt;br&gt;Communicate proactively with the Head of Product, flagging risks early, aligning on priorities, and operating with a high degree of autonomy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;7+ years of apparel design experience with a strong portfolio in lifestyle and athletic categories; kids&#39; wear experience is required&lt;br&gt;Deep fluency in garment construction — you understand how a garment is built and can document it precisely for a factory&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated ability to build or contribute to tech packs, particularly construction and technical specification pages&lt;br&gt;Experience art directing designers and integrating graphic applications into apparel design&lt;br&gt;Strong seasonal planning instincts — you know how to sequence a calendar and manage multiple categories simultaneously&lt;br&gt;A self-starter who operates well without heavy oversight and communicates clearly up and down the org&lt;br&gt;Proficiency in Adobe Illustrator, and Photoshop, and has worked in a PLM system&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Experience at a DTC, digitally native, or creator-led brand&lt;br&gt;Background designing for both kids&#39; and adult markets&lt;br&gt;Experience hiring or scaling a small design team or working with contractors&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Knows and understands the MrBeast consumer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Perks, Why Work On the MrBeast Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are redefining what entertainment and storytelling look like at global scale. Every piece of content we publish reaches millions and influences culture in real time. This is your opportunity to lead the team that decides how those moments come to life across every screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Medical (Blue Cross Blue Shield), Dental, Vision and company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions to employee Health Savings Accounts (HSA)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Plan with Safe Harbor company-matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy and paid company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-provided technology package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation assistance where applicable, including travel and company-provided housing for the first 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;324&quot; data-end=&quot;392&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Turn early-stage ideas into structured, scalable creative programs&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1xyyexd&quot; data-start=&quot;394&quot; data-end=&quot;413&quot;&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;414&quot; data-end=&quot;718&quot;&gt;This role exists to translate high-level creative ideas into structured initiatives that can be executed across the organization. The &lt;strong&gt;Director of Creative Development&lt;/strong&gt; partners closely with the Head of Development to shape new programs, partnerships, and narrative platforms from concept through development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;720&quot; data-end=&quot;955&quot;&gt;You will operate at the intersection of creativity, strategy, and execution. The focus is not on producing individual campaigns, but on building the frameworks, direction, and alignment that allow multiple teams to execute effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
