&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with on-camera talent, brand, and communications teams to keep publishing fast, on voice, and on brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with our YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, and Shorts teams so major launches hit together while X keeps its own distinct voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor conversation and sentiment around the brand, amplifying positive momentum and flagging what needs attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track performance daily, test constantly, and translate platform data into weekly and monthly reporting that drives decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 to 8 years running social media with X or Twitter as your primary platform, and at least 2 years as the named owner of a large account (1M+ followers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked somewhere real-time is the job: a sports league, team, or broadcaster; a major media or streaming brand; a gaming or esports organization; a top creator or entertainment company; or a consumer brand known specifically for X excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write exceptional short-form copy in a distinctive voice and can show posts you wrote that traveled, with the numbers behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have run live coverage under pressure: game days, premieres, launches, or breaking moments, with fast approval loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are clip-native: you can cut short-form video yourself or brief editors with precision, and you know the difference between a clip that travels and one that doesn&#39;t. This is not a pure writing role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how content spreads on the platform, including the creator and community pages that drive distribution, and ideally you bring relationships in that world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well with stakeholders: you know how to keep brand, communications, and leadership aligned while moving at the speed the platform demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent in platform analytics and testing, and you make publishing decisions from data, not instinct alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You live on these platforms, you understand internet culture at a native level, and your judgment holds up at speed.&lt;/li&gt;
