&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play a pivotal role building and leading the company-wide accounts payable and T&amp;amp;E function for Beast Industries; owning the Ramp spend platform, accelerating procure-to-pay, and building rigorous payment controls as the organization continues to scale.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Corporate Controller, the Head of Accounts Payable will own accounts payable and travel &amp;amp; expense across all Beast Industries business units — media production, consumer products, fintech, and emerging ventures — and lead the team that keeps a high-volume, multi-entity payables operation running with accuracy and control. This role owns the Ramp platform end-to-end including corporate cards, bill pay, procurement and T&amp;amp;E workflows, along with vendor management and payment controls. The Head of Accounts Payable will lead and develop an A/P and T&amp;amp;E team while partnering with business leaders to accelerate the procure-to-pay cycle. The ideal candidate is a hands-on operator with deep procure-to-pay expertise and a builder mentality who can accelerate processes and enhance controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end accounts payable across all entities and business units&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Ramp platform: corporate card programs, bill pay workflows, procurement, approval hierarchies, and T&amp;amp;E administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop the A/P and T&amp;amp;E team across locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate the procure-to-pay cycle across vendor onboarding, PO discipline, invoice processing, and payment execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer the company&#39;s T&amp;amp;E and spend policy, including exception management, audits, and policy iteration with Finance leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain rigorous payment controls, including segregation of duties, payment approvals, and fraud prevention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendor master governance: onboarding, W-9/W-8 collection, banking verification, and 1099 reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with treasury workflows on payment runs, cash forecasting inputs, and banking relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive automation across invoice capture, coding, and matching within Ramp and NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key point of contact for external auditors on A/P, T&amp;amp;E, and payment control matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of progressive accounts payable / procure-to-pay experience, including leadership of multi-entity A/P functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA or relevant certification a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise with Ramp and NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building payment controls and segregation of duties&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success accelerating P2P cycle times without sacrificing accuracy or control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing distributed teams with a hands-on, player-coach approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong vendor management instincts, including 1099 compliance and vendor risk practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to partner effectively with non-finance stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, evolving, high-transaction-volume environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The target total compensation ranges from $186,000 – $228,000 including a fixed annual salary of $155,000 – $190,000, an employee equity plan grant, bonus, plus comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equity grants are issued in good faith, subject to company policies, board approval, and individual eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Perks, Why Work On the MrBeast Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are redefining what entertainment and storytelling look like at global scale. Every piece of content we publish reaches millions and influences culture in real time. This is your opportunity to lead the team that decides how those moments come to life across every screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Medical (Blue Cross Blue Shield), Dental, Vision and company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions to employee Health Savings Accounts (HSA)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Plan with Safe Harbor company-matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy and paid company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-provided technology package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation assistance where applicable, including travel and company-provided housing for the first 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a new consumer app that enables our fans to engage in challenges, philanthropy,&amp;nbsp; and other interactive experiences at scale. You&#39;ll be the chief architect of our customer support and platform integrity infrastructure, the systems, workflows, and SOPs that let a small team make consistent decisions at scale, and the vendor stack that powers all of it. You&#39;ll own the full loop: keeping the platform safe and making sure the people who run into problems get taken care of. This is a zero-to-one build. You&#39;re not inheriting a playbook, you&#39;re writing it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end support experience for users, ensuring the platform is safe, fair, and well-supported across every surface&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the operating model end to end: tier structure, severity framework, escalation paths, SLAs, and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the build, buy, and outsource decisions: BPO strategy, vendor selection across support &amp;amp; integrity, and where to invest as the company scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design coverage that reflects the always-on nature of a consumer app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the metrics that drive user retention and brand trust: response and resolution time, CSAT, SLA attainment, deflection, cost to serve, and contest and prize integrity outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up the internal support and integrity tooling and workflows the team runs on&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement, automation, and self-service deflection through AI-augmented workflows that improve both speed and quality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and engineering to ensure we build a trusted, safe, and fair experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align customer support and platform integrity decisions with commercial goals, brand risk, and the expectations of external partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operator at Scale: 12+ years in customer operations with direct ownership of both a customer-facing support function and a safety/fraud function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth Focused: You&#39;ve scaled customer support operations at online platforms with demonstrated, quantifiable impact on both cost efficiency and user experience, and you&#39;ve built or matured billing, collections, or dispute resolution processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulatory Fluent: Direct experience with safety and privacy compliance in a consumer product&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor-Savvy Builder: Hands-on experience selecting and implementing the trust and safety and support vendor landscape (case management and enforcement platforms, bot and fraud prevention etc), and you know when to build in-house instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-Forward: A clear point of view on where AI and automation belong in fraud detection and customer support, and the ability to actually implement that vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Operator: Strong communicator who can build trust with cross functional partners. You are comfortable being the final call on high-stakes escalations, and equally comfortable in the weeds of a messy ticket queue when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Perks, Why Work On the MrBeast Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are redefining what entertainment and storytelling look like at global scale. Every piece of content we publish reaches millions and influences culture in real time. This is your opportunity to lead the team that decides how those moments come to life across every screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Medical (Blue Cross Blue Shield), Dental, Vision and company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company contributions to employee Health Savings Accounts (HSA)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Plan with Safe Harbor company-matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible vacation policy and paid company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-provided technology package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation assistance where applicable, including travel and company-provided housing for the first 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is a multifaceted media and entertainment company founded by Jimmy Donaldson, popularly known as MrBeast, the most watched person in the world. Renowned for revolutionizing digital content creation, Beast Industries encompasses a diverse portfolio of ventures that extend far beyond its origins on YouTube. With a mission to entertain, inspire, and create significant social impact, Beast Industries operates across various domains including digital media, philanthropy, consumer products, and innovative business initiatives. At Beast Industries, we believe in the transformative power of digital media and its potential to entertain, educate, and effect positive change. Our commitment to innovation, creativity, and philanthropy drives us to explore new frontiers, create unforgettable experiences, and build a legacy that inspires future generations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Los Angeles, CA (preferred)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting To:&lt;/strong&gt; GM and President, Beast Studios&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the next generation of creator-led programming.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beast Industries is building a growing direct-to-consumer content business with an expanding portfolio of original programming. As Head of Programming, you&#39;ll define the creative vision, programming strategy, and content roadmap that shapes the member experience and drives long-term engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the GM and President, Beast Studios, you oversee a portfolio of original programming—from flagship series and recurring formats to creator partnerships and our growing content library. You&#39;ll shape what gets made, how our slate evolves, and how programming drives long-term member engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior creative leadership role for someone who has successfully built and managed programming across digital platforms, streaming services, studios, or premium entertainment brands. Working closely with Production, Talent, Product, Marketing, Analytics, and executive leadership, you&#39;ll guide programming from concept through launch while continually evolving the slate through audience insights, creative vision, and business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the programming vision and long-term content strategy across our growing portfolio of original content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a diversified slate of original programming across multiple formats and genres.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new series, recurring formats, creator partnerships, and programming opportunities that strengthen the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee creative development from concept through greenlight, ensuring ideas align with audience needs and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Production to successfully launch programming while maintaining creative quality and execution standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product, Marketing, Analytics, Audience, and executive leadership to inform programming decisions through audience insights and performance data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop programming roadmaps that balance flagship launches, recurring series, evergreen content, and library strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with creators, production partners, agencies, and industry talent to expand programming opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evaluate content performance and evolve the slate based on audience behavior, retention, and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing programming organization as the platform grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading programming, creative development, or original content strategy for a digital platform, streaming service, studio, media company, or creator business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of overseeing multiple productions or programming initiatives simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing unscripted, entertainment, or creator-led content from concept through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative judgment with the ability to identify formats, talent, and ideas that resonate with audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with production, product, marketing, analytics, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-informed approach to creative decision-making, using audience insights to guide programming strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and leadership skills, with the ability to align diverse stakeholders around a creative vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in fast-moving, evolving environments where priorities shift and new opportunities emerge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for digital entertainment, creator culture, and building category-defining programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is &lt;strong&gt;$170,000–$230,000&lt;/strong&gt;, in addition to eligibility for an annual bonus, an equity grant under the company&#39;s employee equity plan, and a comprehensive benefits package.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
