&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1xyyexd&quot; data-start=&quot;312&quot; data-end=&quot;331&quot;&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;332&quot; data-end=&quot;631&quot;&gt;MrBeast is looking for an analytical, strategic, and tech-savvy &lt;strong&gt;Senior HRIS Analyst (Workday) &lt;/strong&gt;to join our General team working on scaling our global HR and IT infrastructure. In this role, you will serve as a techno-functional subject matter expert responsible for designing, optimizing, and maintaining Workday across the entire employee lifecycle. You will thrive in a fast-paced environment, ensuring top-tier data integrity, seamless integrations, and actionable workforce visibility through advanced analytics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;xti9y5&quot; data-start=&quot;1365&quot; data-end=&quot;1385&quot;&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the architectural design, delivery, and ongoing evolution of Workday to support evolving organizational goals across HR, IT, and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary system administrator for Workday Core HCM, managing business process configurations, security roles, and calculated fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and maintain seamless integrations between Workday and external ecosystem tools, including Deel, Greenhouse, Britehire, 15Five, and Okta.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and support robust integrations utilizing Workday Studio, EIBs, and REST/SOAP APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish automated ETL data pipelines using tools like Airbyte or Fivetran to extract Workday data into centralized data warehouses (Snowflake/BigQuery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive executive decision-making by creating advanced reporting solutions, executive dashboards, and leveraging Workday People Analytics and Prism Analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end Workday release management, feature evaluation, and regression testing to ensure continuous operational uptime with zero unhandled production issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business requirements into scalable technical specifications while developing documentation and change management strategies to support user adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1h70sx2&quot; data-start=&quot;2359&quot; data-end=&quot;2382&quot;&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;2383&quot; data-end=&quot;3485&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of total HRIS/HR technology administration experience, with 5+ years of direct, hands-on Workday configuration in mid-sized or fast-growth organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep functional expertise in Workday Core HCM, Compensation, Benefits, and Time Tracking modules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced technical proficiency building integrations using Workday Studio, EIBs, APIs, and managing Workday security architecture (ISUs and security groups).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with SQL, ETL tools (Airbyte or Fivetran), and cloud data warehouses (Snowflake or BigQuery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Workday People Analytics, Prism Analytics, and custom dashboard creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication skills, with a proven ability to bridge the gap between technical specs and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncompromising focus on data integrity, system security, and operational quality under tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced, high-growth environments supporting modern enterprise tools (e.g., Okta, Greenhouse, Deel) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;44&quot; data-end=&quot;237&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;The target total compensation ranges from $200,250 - $278,450 including a fixed annual salary of $135,000– $203,000, an employee equity plan grant, bonus, plus comprehensive benefits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
